# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
# `Shape::circle` — `::` takes a record's own name on its left, and a variant
# has cases rather than fields. It is refused one phase earlier than the other
# four ways of getting `::` wrong, by the rule that a variant names a type and
# not a value, which is why it stands in its own file: a resolve error gates
# the type check, so a file holding this case and the others would report this
# one and leave the rest untested while the suite stayed green.
#
# The message that already existed is the right one and is pinned so it stays.

variant Shape
    circle
    square

function main()
    print(Shape::circle)  #~ variant_in_value_position
